# CodeQL ignore file. One entry per line: `path:query-id`. A bare
# query-id (e.g. `py/clear-text-storage-sensitive-data`) suppresses
# that query on ALL files. A `path:query-id` form suppresses it on
# the specific path.
#
# Intentionally-allowed code patterns:
#
# The PR-39 stress test (gated on R2_* env vars) writes R2
# credentials to a per-invocation tmpfile. The credentials are
# read from environment variables (not hardcoded), the tmpfile
# is mode-600 in a per-invocation mkdtemp() directory, and the
# whole test block is opt-in via env-var presence. The
# r2-lifecycle CLI's only auth option is a credentials file, so
# there's no way to avoid the write without changing the CLI
# itself. The alternative (using SARIF suppressions on every
# run) is a maintenance burden vs. a single .codeqlignore entry.
#
# Suppress the storage-of-credentials finding for the opt-in
# stress test. The actual credential material is not in the
# repo, only the pattern that reads from env and writes to a
# tmpfile.
tests/stress/stress_pr39_real_vastai.py:py/clear-text-storage-sensitive-data
